+# PROGRAM 13C — F-6 · A dev run silently targets production
+
+**13 August 2026** · found while verifying the commands to start the app locally
+· amends `PROGRAM-13C-FINAL-CERTIFICATION.md` §1 (findings) and §2 (evidence pattern)
+
+---
+
+## Statement
+
+`npm run dev` on any tree that has ever run `npm run package` points the desktop
+application at **`https://api.neuropause033.com`**, not at the developer's local
+backend — with no warning, no prompt, and nothing in `git status`.
+
+Severity is not "wrong URL in dev". Sign-in, token refresh, device registration,
+organizations, billing and catalog all resolve through `config.backendUrl`
+(17 call sites). A developer believing they are testing locally is authenticating
+real credentials against, and writing to, the production service.
+
+---
+
+## Mechanism
+
+1. `apps/desktop/scripts/generate-build-info.cjs` writes
+   `apps/desktop/resources/build-info.json` at package time, containing
+   `"backendUrl": "https://api.neuropause033.com"`.
+2. That file is **correctly gitignored** — `.gitignore` carries it under
+   *"Generated at package time by generate-build-info.cjs; never commit"*. Being
+   gitignored is exactly why it is invisible: it never appears in `git status`,
+   survives branch switches, and survives `git clean` without `-x`.
+3. `buildInfo.readGenerated()` resolves it through `app.getAppPath()`. Its header
+   says *"absence is expected in dev"* — but it does not check `app.isPackaged`,
+   and in an `electron-vite dev` run `app.getAppPath()` is `apps/desktop`, so
+   candidate #3 (`<appPath>/resources/build-info.json`) hits.
+4. `config.ts:23` took `getBakedBackendUrl() ?? 'http://127.0.0.1:4000'` as its
+   default. The baked value wins in dev.
+
+Every step is individually reasonable. The defect is only visible where they meet.
+
+---
+
+## Evidence — runtime, not inference
+
+Container with PostgreSQL 16 + Redis 7 + the backend live on `:4000`
+(`/health` → `{"status":"ok","components":{"database":"up","redis":"up"}}`),
+Electron launched headless against the built main process.
+
+| Condition | `Starting in development mode { backendUrl: … }` |
+|---|---|
+| `build-info.json` present, no env var — **before fix** | `https://api.neuropause033.com` |
+| `NEUROPAUSE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000` | `http://127.0.0.1:4000` |
+| `build-info.json` removed, no env var | `http://127.0.0.1:4000` |
+| `build-info.json` present, no env var — **after fix** | `http://127.0.0.1:4000` |
+
+Rows 2 and 3 are the two workarounds available without a code change. Row 4 is
+the fix.
+
+---
+
+## Fix
+
+`config.ts` — a packaged build uses the baked URL (that is what baking is for);
+an unpackaged run defaults to local. `NEUROPAUSE_BACKEND_URL` still overrides in
+both modes, which stays the supported way to point a dev run at staging.
+
+`config.test.ts` — 6 tests. Negative control run: reverting the `app.isPackaged`
+guard makes case 1 fail with
+`expected 'https://api.neuropause033.com' to be 'http://127.0.0.1:4000'`, and
+restoring it returns 6/6. The test is therefore load-bearing, not decorative.
+
+---
+
+## Why this belongs in the certification record
+
+§2 of the certification names one recurring failure: **a status assigned by
+counting a proxy that was easier to measure than the thing.** Three instances were
+already recorded — adapters *written* vs *registered*; declarations vs coverage; a
+component *completing* vs the application *reaching* it.
+
+F-6 is the fourth, and its proxy is the most tempting of the four: *the source
+says the default is `127.0.0.1`.* It does. Reading `config.ts:23` — which I did —
+gives the local URL. Only executing it gives the production one, because the
+deciding input is a gitignored file in the working tree that no reading of the
+repository can see.
+
+**Rule for this class:** a configuration value that depends on filesystem state
+cannot be certified by reading the code that computes it. It has to be printed by
+a running process, in the state the operator will actually be in.
+
+The Round 17 runtime-evidence discipline was applied to features. It was not
+applied to configuration. It is now.
+
+---
+
+## Related, unresolved
+
+- F-4 (the sign-in wall) is unchanged. F-6 explains one way a local backend can be
+  running and the app *still* reports it cannot reach a backend — it was never
+  asked.
+- `neuropause033.com` still has no A record; `api.neuropause033.com` is
+  134.199.250.188. F-6 means dev runs have been reaching the second of those.
+- Any credential typed into a dev run since the first `npm run package` on that
+  tree should be treated as having been sent to production.
